diff --git a/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
index 922deaa53..e099261ea 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
@@ -159,8 +159,8 @@ The server exposes tools across three modules in `crates/app/src/mcp/` (see `cra
 - `generate { "name"?: string }`: Generate toolpaths for a named operation or all stale operations.
 - `verify { "name"?: string }`: Check toolpaths against safety rules (spindle speed, rapids touching material, shaft collision, machine limits).
 - `render_stock { "width"?: number, "height"?: number, "view"?: "iso" | "top" }`: Render simulated stock to a PNG image with rest/gouge color shading.
-- `get_post_options { "setup"?: string | null }`: Read post options (`skip_stops`, `per_op`, `threading`, `end_units`, `smoothing`, `between_setups`, `explain`), `follows_document`, and `own`. With `setup`, reads that declared setup's resolved options; without `setup` (or `null`), reads the document's (#1534).
-- `set_post_options { "setup"?: string | null, "follow"?: boolean, "skip_stops"?: boolean, "per_op"?: boolean, "threading"?: "g32"|"g76", "end_units"?: "leave"|"inch"|"mm", "smoothing"?: boolean, "between_setups"?: "pause"|"optional-stop"|"continue"|"file-per-setup", "explain"?: boolean }`: Set post options as one undoable step (#1534). Target is explicit (no implicit active-setup routing): with `setup`, writes that setup's own options (`SetSetupPostOptions`), or `follow: true` returns it to following the document; without `setup`, writes the document's (`SetPostOptions`). Omitted option fields keep their current values; no-ops and unknown setups/values are refused by name.
+- `get_post_options { "setup"?: string | null }`: Read post options (`skip_stops`, `per_op`, `threading`, `end_units`, `smoothing`, `between_setups`, `explain`), `follows_document`, `own`, `post`, `script_schema`, and resolved `script_options`. With `setup`, reads that declared setup's resolved options; without `setup` (or `null`), reads the document's (#1534, #258).
+- `set_post_options { "setup"?: string | null, "follow"?: boolean, "skip_stops"?: boolean, "per_op"?: boolean, "threading"?: "g32"|"g76", "end_units"?: "leave"|"inch"|"mm", "smoothing"?: boolean, "between_setups"?: "pause"|"optional-stop"|"continue"|"file-per-setup", "explain"?: boolean, "script_options"?: object }`: Set post options and/or per-post `script_options` (pass `null` on a key to reset it to the script default) as one undoable step (#1534, #258). Target is explicit (no implicit active-setup routing): with `setup`, writes that setup's own options, or `follow: true` returns both built-in and script options to following the document; without `setup`, writes the document's. Omitted fields keep their current values; no-ops and unknown setups/values/options are refused by name.
 - `post { "output": string, "post"?: string, "between_setups"?: "pause"|"optional-stop"|"continue"|"file-per-setup" }`: Post-process verified toolpaths into the NC file `output` through a built-in post by name (`"Fanuc"`, `"Haas"`, ...) or a `.cps` path. `between_setups` (#1532) first sets what the program does where it changes setup, as an undoable command: `pause` (the default) writes M0 with a comment naming the next setup, `optional-stop` M1, `continue` runs straight on, and `file-per-setup` writes one program per setup beside `output` (the reply's `files` names them).
 
